WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:06.306
"Choosing the Best Greens to
Boost GLP-1 for Weight Loss"

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:08.475
In my last video,

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:11.712
I showed how starting your day
with a single dose of thylakoids

00:00:11.712 --> 00:00:13.247
increased
feelings of satiety

00:00:13.247 --> 00:00:15.849
and decreased hunger and
cravings for snacks and sweets

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:17.518
throughout the day.

00:00:17.518 --> 00:00:19.753
We’re talking about
a powdered spinach extract

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:22.489
equivalent to just half a cup
(80 g) of cooked greens.

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:25.225
Significantly less desire
for salty snacks

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:27.427
over the next nine hours
compared to placebo,

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:29.363
with just one dose of greens.

00:00:29.363 --> 00:00:32.766
Significantly less desire
for sweet snacks, sweet and fat,

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:34.801
snacks in general.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:37.037
Thylakoids, thus,
provide a powerful strategy

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:40.707
to suppress the urge
for so-called "palatable" food,

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:43.810
potato chips, chocolate,
cinnamon buns, and the like.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.546
But despite the lower hunger
and greater satiety,

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:49.816
food intake throughout the day
was not significantly affected.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:52.119
In a systematic review
of randomized clinical trials

00:00:52.119 --> 00:00:53.654
on the effects
of thylakoid intake

00:00:53.654 --> 00:00:55.222
on appetite and weight loss,

00:00:55.222 --> 00:00:57.157
the hunger-suppressing effects
of thylakoids

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:59.493
were reported
in all the relevant studies,

00:00:59.493 --> 00:01:02.362
but what about
the weight-loss part?

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:03.897
Instead of a single dose
of greens,

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:07.234
what about the same dose
every day for three months?

00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:08.669
The title gives it away:

00:01:08.669 --> 00:01:11.571
you get a loss of body weight,
reduced cravings,

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:12.472
and increased release

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:15.375
of the appetite-suppressing
hormone GLP-1.

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:16.710
The average amount
of weight loss

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:18.512
was only about three pounds
(1 kg),

00:01:18.512 --> 00:01:20.047
but the study participants
also got

00:01:20.047 --> 00:01:23.150
a significant drop
in cholesterol of 20 points,

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:24.418
and, as you can see,

00:01:24.418 --> 00:01:27.120
the drop in cholesterol preceded
significant weight loss;

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.255
so, the cholesterol benefit

00:01:28.255 --> 00:01:30.824
wasn’t just because
weight was being lost.

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:32.459
And 20 points?

00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:33.694
That’s the kind
of result you get

00:01:33.694 --> 00:01:36.930
using an earlier class
of cholesterol-lowering drugs.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:41.535
GLP-1 was also boosted by about
40 percent, and check this out:

00:01:41.535 --> 00:01:44.104
significantly lower
cravings for sweets

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:46.974
even 11 hours
after spinach intake.

00:01:46.974 --> 00:01:49.009
And, remember,
the spinach powder was hidden;

00:01:49.009 --> 00:01:50.944
so, people didn’t know
which group they were in,

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:53.347
didn’t know if they were getting
greens or placebo.

00:01:53.347 --> 00:01:56.450
And 11 hours later,
they were, like, chocolate?

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.118
Eh, no thanks.

00:01:58.118 --> 00:02:00.620
Uh, got any spinach?

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.656
So, not only were there
decreased cravings

00:02:02.656 --> 00:02:04.691
in the six hours
prior to lunch,

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:07.094
but also decreased cravings
afterwards--

00:02:07.094 --> 00:02:09.830
all from just getting
that one single dose of greens

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:11.231
in the morning.

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:14.601
That’s the power of GLP-1.

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:16.937
Now, one of the authors
had a conflict of interest,

00:02:16.937 --> 00:02:19.639
affiliations with companies
trying to commercialize

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:20.874
thylakoid products,

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:23.243
and you can see it in the spin.

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:24.745
They described
the spinach extract

00:02:24.745 --> 00:02:27.280
as markedly
reducing body weight,

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:30.951
but I wouldn’t consider
three pounds (1 kg) "markedly."

00:02:30.951 --> 00:02:32.919
They boast that
the 6 percent weight loss

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:36.323
was comparable to an older GLP-1
drug available at the time,

00:02:36.323 --> 00:02:39.526
suggesting that increasing
the natural release of GLP-1

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:42.095
may be as efficient
as pharmacological agents

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:44.064
for the treatment for obesity.

00:02:44.064 --> 00:02:46.566
Of course, our new GLP-1 drugs

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:49.302
can decrease body weight
by more than 6 percent,

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:51.171
but the 6 percent loss
in this study

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:54.174
was from baseline,
not compared to placebo.

00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:57.310
Those on the placebo lost about
4 percent of their body weight;

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.846
so, weight loss
attributable to the spinach

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:02.649
was more like only 2 percent.

00:03:02.649 --> 00:03:05.218
And another eight-week study
found no significant difference

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:06.286
at all.

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:07.287
So, when they took
their supplement

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:08.522
to the European equivalent

00:03:08.522 --> 00:03:10.223
of the U.S. Food and Drug
Administration

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:12.526
to try to make
a weight-loss health claim,

00:03:12.526 --> 00:03:15.328
the panel was, like,
a 1 percent weight loss?

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:17.464
That’s really not going
to do much.

00:03:17.464 --> 00:03:19.900
Whether these appetite-lowering
effects of thylakoids

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:21.201
could be a useful strategy

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:22.703
in controlling obesity
in the long term

00:03:22.703 --> 00:03:23.770
is still ambiguous.

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.539
More studies are needed.

00:03:25.539 --> 00:03:30.177
And, here we go, the latest
thylakoid weight loss study.

00:03:30.177 --> 00:03:32.279
A randomized, double-blind,
placebo-controlled trial

00:03:32.279 --> 00:03:33.914
with that same dose

00:03:33.914 --> 00:03:35.916
equivalent to half a cup (80 g)
of cooked greens,

00:03:35.916 --> 00:03:39.519
and there was a significant
decrease in body weight,

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:42.222
fat mass, waist circumference,
waist-to-height ratio,

00:03:42.222 --> 00:03:45.625
and body mass index (BMI)
compared to placebo--

00:03:45.625 --> 00:03:47.994
and, by a decent amount.

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:51.498
Individuals in the spinach group
lost 15 pounds (7 kg),

00:03:51.498 --> 00:03:53.500
compared to 7
in the placebo group.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:55.802
Eight more pounds (3 kg)
of weight loss on greens

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:56.937
than placebo.

00:03:56.937 --> 00:03:59.272
And that included
8 pounds of straight fat,

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:02.275
including 4 more centimeters
off the waist.

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:04.377
So, based on a systematic review

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:06.279
of the potential effects
of thylakoids

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:08.081
in the management of obesity,

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:11.852
eating green can suppress
hunger, reduce food intake,

00:04:11.852 --> 00:04:13.587
and result in weight loss.

00:04:13.587 --> 00:04:16.490
Greens can offer a means
to strengthen our resolve

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:18.024
to refrain from eating,

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:21.061
especially when we’re in a kind
of high-doughnut environment

00:04:21.061 --> 00:04:23.029
where there is
"superfluous access

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:25.165
to foods processed
to deliver qualities

00:04:25.165 --> 00:04:28.034
that some may find
irresistible."

00:04:28.034 --> 00:04:28.902
It’s interesting,

00:04:28.902 --> 00:04:31.938
even supplementing a breakfast
that was only 11 percent fat

00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:35.175
with thylakoids resulted in
decreased hunger and cravings,

00:04:35.175 --> 00:04:37.210
suggesting that there
might be other mechanisms

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:39.346
for the appetite-suppressive
effect of thylakoids

00:04:39.346 --> 00:04:42.249
beyond just slowing
the digestion of fat.

00:04:42.249 --> 00:04:44.985
Here are some of the proposed
mechanisms aside from GLP-1

00:04:44.985 --> 00:04:47.721
that may be contributing
to weight loss.

00:04:47.721 --> 00:04:49.990
Regardless, what’s the best way
to get them?

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:53.760
Not from the supplement aisle,
but rather the produce aisle.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:56.696
And remember, that’s where
the chlorophyll is found;

00:04:56.696 --> 00:04:58.465
so, you can see
with your own eyes

00:04:58.465 --> 00:05:00.300
which veggies
have more thylakoids

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:03.136
by how dark green they are.

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:05.305
What happens
when you cook greens?

00:05:05.305 --> 00:05:08.675
Blanched for 15 seconds or so
in steaming or boiling water,

00:05:08.675 --> 00:05:10.710
they actually get
even brighter green,

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.012
but if you cook them too long,

00:05:12.012 --> 00:05:14.548
they eventually turn
a drab olive brown.

00:05:14.548 --> 00:05:15.949
When greens are overcooked,

00:05:15.949 --> 00:05:18.051
their thylakoids
physically degrade,

00:05:18.051 --> 00:05:20.520
along with their ability
to slow fat absorption.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.255
Within that first minute
of cooking,

00:05:22.255 --> 00:05:24.124
when the green gets
even more vibrant, though,

00:05:24.124 --> 00:05:26.893
there’s a slight boost
in fat-blocking ability.

00:05:26.893 --> 00:05:29.829
So, you can gauge
thylakoid activity

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:31.932
in both the grocery store
and in your kitchen

00:05:31.932 --> 00:05:34.968
with your own two eyes.

00:05:34.968 --> 00:05:38.705
We have been chewing on leaves
for millions of years,

00:05:38.705 --> 00:05:39.906
but today,

00:05:39.906 --> 00:05:42.542
the greenest thing
about some people’s diets

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:45.412
may be a St. Patty’s Day pint.

00:05:45.412 --> 00:05:49.349
Americans have averaged fewer
than two grams of spinach a day,

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:50.984
not even half a teaspoon.

00:05:50.984 --> 00:05:52.986
But our bodies were designed
to have thylakoids

00:05:52.986 --> 00:05:56.122
passing through our systems
on a daily basis;

00:05:56.122 --> 00:05:58.825
so, that delay in fat absorption
we get from them

00:05:58.825 --> 00:06:02.095
can be thought of
as our default, normal state.

00:06:02.095 --> 00:06:05.565
It’s only when we eat diets
deficient in greens

00:06:05.565 --> 00:06:07.634
that we suffer
the accelerated fat digestion

00:06:07.634 --> 00:06:11.204
that undercuts
our natural satiety mechanisms.

00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:13.974
In the journal of the Society
of Chemical Industry,

00:06:13.974 --> 00:06:16.376
a group of food technologists
argued that,

00:06:16.376 --> 00:06:18.311
given their
fat-blocking benefits,

00:06:18.311 --> 00:06:19.613
"thylakoid membranes

00:06:19.613 --> 00:06:21.248
could be incorporated
in functional foods

00:06:21.248 --> 00:06:24.317
as a new promising
appetite-reducing ingredient,"

00:06:24.317 --> 00:06:29.222
or you can just get them
the way Mother Nature intended.

